Heidenfeld refused")} 33. Qf5 Qe6 34. Qh5 Nc3 35. Rc1 Rxa3 36. Qc5 Qb3 37. Bh6
Rd8 {"and now, with three moves to make in half a minute, Heidenfeld produced}
38. Qc7 $4 (38. h3 $1 $18) {"There was distant thunder along the beaches of
Blackpool as Barden banged down..."} 38... Rd1+ 39. Bf1 Qd5+ {Sources: CHESS,
October 1956, p23; BCM, October 1956, p262 (with Heidenfeld's own comments)}
0-1

